            <ArticleTitle>Total hip replacement with a straight stem prosthesis. A 2-year follow-up of 126 CAD operations.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>146-51</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The clinical and radiographic results in 126 primary CAD total hip replacements were assessed after 2 years in a prospective study. The clinical overall results were satisfactory, with 89 per cent of the hips being free from significant pain. Femoral component loosening was radiographically evident in 6 per cent. The walking speed was increased by 83 per cent in patients with unilateral hip disease. This increase was partly achieved during the second postoperative year.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
